# Netlify SPA fallback — every path that isn't an existing file serves
# Index.html so client-side path routing works for deep links like
# packs.ink/decks, packs.ink/screener, packs.ink/analytics, etc.
#
# Logos/ must serve its own image files (used at runtime), so list it first so
# it doesn't fall through to the SPA shell.
/Logos/*  /Logos/:splat  200

# Internal source/docs are committed at the publish root and would otherwise be
# served verbatim (Netlify serves an existing file before the SPA fallback). The
# site never fetches these at runtime, so force a 404 (the trailing ! overrides
# the on-disk file) to keep ops docs / ETL scripts / migration SQL / the MCP
# config off the public web. Add new internal paths here if they ship to root.
/CLAUDE.md    /Index.html  404!
/handoff.md   /Index.html  404!
/.mcp.json    /Index.html  404!
/scripts/*    /Index.html  404!
/supabase/*   /Index.html  404!

# Image proxy: Lorcast's CDN doesn't send CORS headers, so direct <img> loads
# can't be drawn to a canvas (needed for the Export Deck Image feature). Proxying
# through our origin makes the response same-origin → canvas-friendly.
/img-proxy/*  https://cards.lorcast.io/:splat  200

# Same for TCGPlayer's CDN — used for Lorcast-unindexed promo/extras cards
# (synthetic catalog rows) and sealed-product art. Their image host also omits
# CORS headers, so without this proxy those cards render blank in canvas exports
# (mover banners/tiles, card/deck posters) even though they display fine on-page.
/tcg-img-proxy/*  https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/:splat  200

# Pretty URL for the standalone privacy policy. /privacy.html is the real file;
# /privacy maps to it so the link looks clean. (Google's OAuth consent
# verification reads this URL from the Branding form and scrapes it without
# running JavaScript — having it as a real HTML file is what makes the check
# pass, vs. the in-app /how-it-works#privacy SPA route.)
/privacy  /privacy.html  200

# Everything else falls through to Index.html with HTTP 200, leaving the
# original path in window.location.pathname so the app can parse it.
/*  /Index.html  200
